  "summary": [
    "Context: the old read-only selector design conflicted with the agent data exchange rule requiring script-written JSON",
    "Why the decision lives in a design doc rather than going back to requirements, with the user approval quoted",
    "Decision: give the selector Bash and pass results through a script as JSON with an exit value",
    "Write prohibition is enforced by Role constraints and the handoff script checking paths against the built-in index",
    "Configuration matches the DES-072 reviewer, a read-only custom agent with Bash",
    "Rejected alternative: keep read-only with return values as an exception to the exchange rule, and why it was rejected",
    "Impacts: the exchange pattern now matches other agents, and write safety no longer relies on tool permissions",
    "Links to DES-090 sections 6, 8.3, 8.9 and to REQ-035"
  ],
